SwiftPutty local patch 0009
Upstream: PuTTY 0.85 (a3cce3a48d4ab12e0fccb32998b9042d4f7c3ff1)
Status:   reported upstream (2026-10-19); suitable for upstream

Free the Rlogin user name prompt once it has been answered.

When no remote user name is configured, rlogin asks for one in the
terminal ("rlogin username:"). rlogin_startup() then sends the greeting
using the answer and sets rlogin->prompt to NULL (which tells
rlogin_sendok() that input may flow), but never frees the prompts_t, so
rlogin_free() cannot free it either: every such login leaked the prompt
and its strings. Found with `leaks --atExit` (Core/tests/spb_backends_test.c).

Free it before forgetting it; the answer has already been written to
the socket.

--- a/otherbackends/rlogin.c
+++ b/otherbackends/rlogin.c
@@ -194,7 +194,12 @@
         rlogin->bufsize = sk_write(rlogin->s, &z, 1);
     }
 
-    rlogin->prompt = NULL;
+    /* The user name prompt (if any) is answered and finished with: the
+     * result has been sent above. */
+    if (rlogin->prompt) {
+        free_prompts(rlogin->prompt);
+        rlogin->prompt = NULL;
+    }
     if (rlogin->ldisc)
         ldisc_check_sendok(rlogin->ldisc);
 }
